  <section class="hcm-fr-section" id="editorial">
    <div class="hcm-fr-wrap-sm">
      <div class="hcm-fr-hd"><span class="hcm-fr-eyebrow">Expert Analysis</span><h2>Expert Editorial Summary: Fujiiryoki Massage Chair Reviews</h2></div>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px">After working with buyers exploring Fujiiryoki massage chairs — from first-time premium shoppers to experienced upgraders seeking Japanese engineering quality — the HCM product team has observed clear, consistent patterns in how customers experience the brand.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">General Customer Satisfaction:</strong> Fujiiryoki massage chairs earn strong satisfaction from customers who value massage precision and mechanical quality over feature quantity. The brand's defining strength is its Japanese engineering heritage — over 70 years of massage chair development that translates directly into how the massage feels.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Strongest Features:</strong> Three features consistently rise to the top: <span class="hcm-fr-mark">precision mechanical massage quality</span>, <span class="hcm-fr-mark">Japanese engineering build durability</span>, and <span class="hcm-fr-mark">AI-guided body scanning</span> (Cyber Relax AI).</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Most Common Expectation Gaps:</strong> The most frequent gap involves massage intensity — first-time users may find it stronger than expected. Foot roller intensity is the second-most common consideration. Design aesthetics may feel more functional than decorative for some homes.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Pre-Purchase Recommendations:</strong></p>
