  <section class="hcm-fr-section hcm-fr-alt" id="faq">
    <div class="hcm-fr-wrap-sm">
      <div class="hcm-fr-hd center"><span class="hcm-fr-eyebrow">Frequently Asked</span><h2>Fujiiryoki Massage Chair Reviews FAQ</h2></div>
      <div class="hcm-fr-faq">
        <details><summary>Are Fujiiryoki massage chairs good?</summary><div><p>Yes — Fujiiryoki is the original Japanese massage chair brand, established in 1954 with over 70 years of continuous engineering innovation. Customers consistently rate Fujiiryoki highly for massage precision, mechanical quality, Japanese engineering, and long-term build durability. The key to satisfaction is choosing the right model. An <a href="{{ shop.url }}/pages/contact">HCM product specialist</a> can help match you to the best-fit model.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>What do customers say in Fujiiryoki massage chair reviews?</summary><div><p>Common themes include strong satisfaction with massage performance, precise mechanical quality, Japanese engineering feel, durable build quality, and consistent long-term ownership experience. Areas of mixed feedback include foot roller intensity for sensitive users and massage intensity feeling strong at first. Overall sentiment is strongly positive, particularly among daily users who value precision.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Are Fujiiryoki massage chairs worth it?</summary><div><p>For buyers who value massage quality and Japanese engineering over maximum feature density, Fujiiryoki consistently delivers strong long-term value. Daily users often describe the investment as worthwhile after experiencing the consistent, precise massage feel over months of use. The MR-6000 Calm Plus offers an accessible entry point starting at $3,999.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>What are the most common Fujiiryoki massage chair complaints?</summary><div><p>The most mentioned considerations are: (1) massage intensity may feel strong at first — start at lower settings, (2) foot rollers can feel intense for sensitive users, (3) premium pricing requires commitment, (4) larger models need space planning, and (5) design is more functional than decorative. These are expectation-management areas, not quality issues.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Is Fujiiryoki good for back comfort and relaxation?</summary><div><p>Many customers report noticeable improvements in back, neck, and shoulder comfort with regular Fujiiryoki use. The precision body scan, SL-Track roller system, and targeted massage programs provide comprehensive coverage. <strong>Important:</strong> massage chairs are comfort and wellness devices, not medical treatment equipment.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Which Fujiiryoki massage chair is best for daily use?</summary><div><p>For daily comfort routines, the <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/fujiiryoki-cyber-relax-elite-massage-chair">Cyber Relax Elite</a> and <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/fujiiryoki-cyber-relax-ai-massage-chair">Cyber Relax AI</a> are frequently recommended. The <a href="{{ shop.url }}/products/mr-6000-calm-plus-fujiiryoki-massage-chair">MR-6000 Calm Plus</a> offers accessible daily Japanese quality. Trying different models at an <a href="{{ shop.url }}/pages/our-store">HCM showroom</a> is the best way to compare.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Are Fujiiryoki massage chairs strong?</summary><div><p>Yes — Fujiiryoki delivers strong, precise massage performance that users describe as mechanically consistent and controlled. The intensity is adjustable across all models. First-time users may find the default intensity stronger than expected. Starting at lower settings and gradually increasing is recommended.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Are Fujiiryoki foot rollers too intense?</summary><div><p>The foot rollers are effective and well-engineered, but some users may find them strong initially. Most customers adapt within the first week at lower settings. Wearing socks during the first few sessions can help. If foot sensitivity is a concern, we recommend trying the foot roller feature at one of our showrooms before purchasing.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How long do Fujiiryoki massage chairs last?</summary><div><p>Fujiiryoki chairs are built with Japanese engineering standards and durable materials designed for daily use. Customers with extended ownership consistently report consistent massage quality and build integrity. Fujiiryoki chairs come with manufacturer warranty coverage, and HCM provides ongoing support.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Are Fujiiryoki massage chairs good for seniors?</summary><div><p>Yes — Fujiiryoki's auto programs and adjustable intensity settings make them suitable for senior users. The MR-6000 Calm Plus is particularly popular for senior users due to its accessible controls and comfortable lower-intensity settings. Starting at lower intensity and using guided programs is recommended.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Is Fujiiryoki a Japanese massage chair brand?</summary><div><p>Yes — Fujiiryoki was established in Japan in 1954 and is credited with producing one of the world's earliest massage chairs. The brand represents over 70 years of Japanese massage chair engineering, precision craftsmanship, and continuous innovation in massage technology.</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>Where should I buy a Fujiiryoki massage chair?</summary><div><p>For the best experience, purchase from an <strong>authorized Fujiiryoki dealer</strong> like House of Massage Chairs. This ensures genuine products, valid warranty, professional delivery, and specialist guidance. HCM offers Fujiiryoki chairs at our <a href="{{ shop.url }}/pages/our-store">San Jose showroom</a> (Westfield Oakridge) and Pleasanton showroom (Stoneridge Mall).</p></div></details>
        <details><summary>How do I choose the right Fujiiryoki massage chair?</summary><div><p>Consider your primary use case (daily comfort, athletic recovery, AI precision, or accessible entry), your space, your intensity preference, and your budget. The Cyber Relax Pro is the flagship with dual 4D rollers. The Cyber Relax AI offers AI-guided personalization. The Elite focuses on leg relief. The MR-6000 is the accessible entry. <a href="{{ shop.url }}/pages/our-store">Visit our showroom</a> to compare all four.</p></div></details>
      </div>
      <div class="hcm-fr-disclaimer">These FAQ answers are based on common customer feedback themes, HCM product specialist observations, and general manufacturer information. They do not constitute medical advice. Fujiiryoki massage chairs are comfort and wellness devices.</div>
